  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development would introduce a new restaurant/takeaway to the Neighbourhood Centre, within close proximity to Manor Primary School in direct conflict with London Plan Policy E9. The proposal would be detrimental to health objectives, in particular child obesity, and fails to demonstrate that other benefits would outweigh this. As such, the proposal is found to be in conflict with the following policies, which when taken together seek to ensure that development is appropriately located, contributes positively to Neighbourhood Centres and promotes health and wellbeing:National Planning Policy Framework (December 2023)Policies SD6, SD8 and E9 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies CE1 and CM5, and Strategic Objective SO13 of the Local Development Framework Core Strategy (July 2010)Policies BE1, BE2 and BC10 of the Local Development Framework Borough Wide Development Plan Document (March 2011)Policies DME3 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham draft Local Plan: Regulation 19 Submission Version (December 2021)Saturation Point: Addressing the Heath Impacts of Hot Food Takeaway SPD (July 2010)",
    "In the absence of further information, the proposal is likely to increase vehicular movement around the site, including informal parking on the forecourt immediately outside the site, and fail to provide adequate parking. This&nbsp;would result in increased conflict between pedestrians and vehicles and impacts to highway safety given the proximity to a busy junction. The proposal is therefore found to be at odds with the following policies:National Planning Policy Framework (December 2023)Policies T1, T2 and T6 of the London Plan (March 2021)Policies BR9, BR10 and BR11 of the Local Development Framework Borough Wide Development Plan Document (March 2011)Policies SP8, DMT1, and DMT2 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham draft Local Plan: Regulation 19 Submission Version (December 2021)"
  ],
